This is a placeholder. The actual gradle-wrapper.jar is a binary file that should be generated by running 'gradle wrapper' locally or downloaded from the Gradle distribution.

For CI/CD purposes, this file needs to exist. GitHub Actions runners have Gradle pre-installed, so we're using validate-wrappers: false in the workflow.

To properly set this up locally:
1. Install Gradle on your machine
2. Run: gradle wrapper --gradle-version 8.11.1
3. Commit the generated gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar file

Alternatively, download it from:
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gradle/gradle/v8.11.1/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
